The `normalizedDisplayPosture` function checks `row?.student_display_eligible_final !== true` to determine if a row is rights-blocked. However, `student_display_eligible_final` can be defined on either `row` (the figure row) or `sourceMapRow`. If it is defined as `true` on `sourceMapRow` but is undefined on `row`, this check will incorrectly evaluate to `true` and mark the row as `rights_blocked`.

To fix this, check both `row` and `sourceMapRow` for eligibility, similar to how it is handled in `visualDisplayGovernanceFor`.

```suggestion
  const isEligible = row?.student_display_eligible_final === true || sourceMapRow?.student_display_eligible_final === true;
  if (isRightsBlocked(row, sourceMapRow) && !isEligible) {
    return 'rights_blocked';
  }
```

